WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.760
Every "Fast and Furious" film has provoked
squabbles among fans, and those squabbles

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.909
have only gotten bigger as the franchise has
grown.

00:00:07.909 --> 00:00:12.880
From casting decisions to plot twists, these
are the times the "Fast and Furious" franchise

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.000
outraged fans the most.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Every "Fast &amp; Furious" movie is a micro time
capsule of what was hot in popular culture

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.319
at the time of its filming.

00:00:21.319 --> 00:00:25.960
The original film was in the dead center of
a time when light wash jeans, Hollister shirts,

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:29.980
and massive aftermarket spoilers were a significant
part of the culture.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.800
The early films were so beholden to trends
that they made an entire movie without the

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:38.900
original cast just to cash in on the surging
popularity of a Japanese racing style.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:43.360
The casting of Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson was
an unquestionably smart decision, but will

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:47.480
also serve as a glimpse of a time when the
wrestler-turned-actor was coming into the

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.222
peak of his box-office powers.

00:00:49.222 --> 00:00:50.179
"I thought so."

00:00:50.179 --> 00:00:53.864
Other casting decisions didn't receive the
same sort of love as Johnson's.

00:00:53.864 --> 00:00:58.860
Fans absolutely lost it when they realized
that rapper Iggy Azalea played a small part

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:02.430
in"Furious 7" and they took to the internet
to vent about it.

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:06.619
Though the part was inconsequential and the
film was still a hit, some people admitted

00:01:06.619 --> 00:01:08.863
it made them properly angry.

00:01:08.863 --> 00:01:13.159
Glasgow is a working-class city, full of the
exact kind of folks that would delight in

00:01:13.159 --> 00:01:16.281
the "Fast" gang's constant heists from greedy
companies.

00:01:16.281 --> 00:01:20.720
However, being a worker means having to get
up in the morning, and the shooting of "Fast

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.602
and Furious 6" made that more than a little
difficult.

00:01:23.602 --> 00:01:28.539
According to reports from the Daily Record,
locals were furious about two weeks of nighttime

00:01:28.539 --> 00:01:33.590
filming that included loud, car-based stunts,
explosions and gunfire.

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:36.840
They took umbrage at the fact that they had
not been warned of the night shoots until

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:40.121
right before they began, and complained repeatedly.

00:01:40.121 --> 00:01:44.250
Glasgow's Film Office painted a different
picture, saying that the film crew behind

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.723
the movie had given residents ample warning.

00:01:46.723 --> 00:01:49.551
At least the stunts looked good on the big
screen.

00:01:49.551 --> 00:01:54.209
While most franchise fans would be ecstatic
at the idea of a new film, a number of people

00:01:54.209 --> 00:01:58.729
in the "Fast" fanbase thought it was crass
when the franchise opted to continue after

00:01:58.729 --> 00:02:00.692
the death of a core cast member.

00:02:00.692 --> 00:02:04.689
Given the focus on family, quite a few fans
were angry when "Fate of the Furious" was

00:02:04.689 --> 00:02:06.898
announced as the eighth film in the series.

00:02:06.898 --> 00:02:10.879
Continuing the series without Paul Walker
didn't sit right with people who had followed

00:02:10.879 --> 00:02:16.473
the franchise from small-scale drag racing
caper to international gang of car-driving superheroes.

00:02:16.802 --> 00:02:20.599
Some fans claimed they would never see the
film, while others simply worried on social

00:02:20.599 --> 00:02:26.450
media that carrying on after Walker's emotional
sendoff would cheapen the ending of "Furious 7."

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:30.640
Still, "Fate" was a hit, and a ninth film
was announced after its release.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:35.241
"Fate of the Furious" gave fans more reasons
to be angry than Paul Walker's absence.

00:02:35.241 --> 00:02:39.290
The plot of the eighth installment in the
series pitted Dominic Toretto against his

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:42.339
surrogate family, which the trailers made
clear.

00:02:42.339 --> 00:02:46.438
Since the movies all stress the importance
of created families and friendly bonds, and

00:02:46.438 --> 00:02:51.209
Toretto has put his life on the line countless
times to save his crew, Dom turning his back

00:02:51.209 --> 00:02:56.005
on that and even threatening to kill his friends
sparked anger when the trailer was released.

00:02:56.005 --> 00:03:00.200
Fans wondered aloud why the franchise would
take such a turn, particularly in the wake

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:04.819
of the loss of Paul Walker in the real world
and the loss of friendly characters like Han

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:06.403
within the "Fast" universe.

00:03:06.403 --> 00:03:09.420
For certain viewers, it felt like the end
of a beloved story.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:12.519
"You lost the minute you interrupted my honeymoon."

00:03:12.519 --> 00:03:17.316
Of course, it was later revealed that Dom's
turn in "Fate" was only part of a blackmail scheme.

00:03:17.316 --> 00:03:21.750
By the end of the film he'd returned to his
family, defeated the bad guys, and even made

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:24.095
time for a cookout with all his friends.

00:03:24.095 --> 00:03:27.154
Han didn't need to be avenged, but fans couldn't
have known that.

00:03:27.154 --> 00:03:31.689
Since "Furious 7," we've been operating under
the assumption that the fan favorite character

00:03:31.689 --> 00:03:36.310
died at the hands of Deckard Shaw, the mercenary
who arrived in that film to avenge his brother's

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:38.867
own defeat in "Fast and Furious 6."

00:03:38.867 --> 00:03:43.200
Shaw's quest for vengeance began with Han,
whose seemingly fatal crash all the way back

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:47.939
in "Tokyo Drift," was revealed to be the same
crash that launched Deckard's fight against

00:03:47.939 --> 00:03:51.900
the Toretto crew in a cliffhanger scene from
"Fast and Furious 6."

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:56.689
Then came "Fate of the Furious," and the revelation
that Deckard Shaw was not only walking free

00:03:56.689 --> 00:04:00.366
after Han's death, but actually becoming part
of the Toretto gang.

00:04:00.366 --> 00:04:04.569
He even landed his own spinoff alongside Dwayne
Johnson's character, Luke Hobbs.

00:04:04.569 --> 00:04:08.799
Han may not have been the most important member
of the Toretto crew, but his death was still

00:04:08.799 --> 00:04:13.359
supposed to mean something, and letting Shaw
just get away with it inspired what's become

00:04:13.359 --> 00:04:19.187
known as the "Justice for Han" movement among
fans, something that will now be addressed in "F9."

00:04:19.187 --> 00:04:23.389
With the "Fast" universe continuing to expand,
some of the sniping over the films is coming

00:04:23.389 --> 00:04:24.848
from inside the franchise.

00:04:24.848 --> 00:04:29.400
Following "Fate of the Furious," series star
Tyrese Gibson tore into the production of

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:34.050
"Hobbs &amp; Shaw," the first movie outside of
the franchise's main timeline, saying that

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:37.042
the film was not worth splitting from the
official series.

00:04:37.042 --> 00:04:41.210
In a now-deleted Instagram post after the
spinoff was released, Gibson tore into the

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:45.650
film's box office numbers and its attempt
at, quote, "breaking up the family."

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:50.280
He also offered the opportunity for "Hobbs
&amp; Shaw" stars Dwayne Johnson and Jason Statham

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:54.415
to return for "Fast 10" to give, quote, "true
fans" what they wanted.

00:04:54.415 --> 00:04:59.440
Gibson's comments only served to stoke reports
of on-set feuding between himself, Johnson,

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.104
Statham, and Vin Diesel.

00:05:01.104 --> 00:05:05.550
At the moment, everyone seems to be happy
with the direction of their careers, but who

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:10.020
knows what the future might hold as the main
"Furious" series reaches its end.

